Reference harness patch, not crate code.

`mpi_enc_test` hard-codes High profile with CABAC and transform-8x8 for H.264 in
both the 2024-04 vintage and current master, and it applies those after any
`-cfg` file, so the cfg keys for `cabac_en` / `profile` have no effect. The
Constrained Baseline job this crate replays - profile_idc 66, level_idc 30,
CAVLC, no transform-8x8 - therefore cannot be requested from the stock harness.

Patching the four lines gives a C encoder that writes the same SPS. What is NOT
steered by the patch is the payload: whether the hardware-coded IDR slice comes
out byte-identical is the actual measurement, and the register diff from
tools/vepu580_trace_diff.py shows any remaining configuration difference instead
of hiding it.

--- a/test/mpi_enc_test.c
+++ b/test/mpi_enc_test.c
@@
-        mpp_enc_cfg_set_s32(cfg, "h264:profile", 100);
+        mpp_enc_cfg_set_s32(cfg, "h264:profile", 66);
@@
-        mpp_enc_cfg_set_s32(cfg, "h264:level", 40);
-        mpp_enc_cfg_set_s32(cfg, "h264:cabac_en", 1);
+        mpp_enc_cfg_set_s32(cfg, "h264:level", 30);
+        mpp_enc_cfg_set_s32(cfg, "h264:cabac_en", 0);
         mpp_enc_cfg_set_s32(cfg, "h264:cabac_idc", 0);
-        mpp_enc_cfg_set_s32(cfg, "h264:trans8x8", 1);
+        mpp_enc_cfg_set_s32(cfg, "h264:trans8x8", 0);
